<title>BELGIUM: EU ministers holding bilateral talks on lira.</title>
<headline>EU ministers holding bilateral talks on lira.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union finance ministers and central bank heads were holding bilateral negotiations during the ongoing meeting on readmitting the lira to the Exchange Rate Mechanism, an official said.</p>
<p>The talks, centring on the rate entry for the lira, have dragged on since early afternoon as a majority of ministers opposed Italy's wish to peg the lira at a rate of 1,000 or weaker to the mark.</p>
<p>Germany was said to demand a much stronger lira level, at 970 lira to the mark. In scarce quoting on the market at around 1940 GMT, the lira inched up to 992.50/3.50 from 998.50 close on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
